Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:37:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST Economy 0041: StrikeList, the strike book follows
 the expert list strictly (on Personality's lists, da1a760)

The user (via the lead): "this is why we looked up expert build orders. literally just
follow the list." New flag StrikeList (off in the bundle). Reads Personality's
CvStrikePlan lists (aBuilds/iNumBuilds, aeTechs/iNumTechs with STRIKE_TECH_LUXURY).

From strike state PREP to the declaration (IsStrikePending), the capital builds the
first list item still short. Each item is one build, and repeats add up per class. Counts
are built units: not the starting ones; upgraded ones and settlers that founded cities
count. So a lost unit is rebuilt in its place. No settler holds, no gold check.
Deviations: the city in danger (a melee defender from the plan); an item the game can't
do yet (passed over, logged LIST WAIT). After the list and in the other cities: the
plan's core, support and siege to the plan's counts (a worker first where a city has
none in its area), then more core while affordable. A late strike in its economy-first
PREP uses the regular book after the list. Research follows aeTechs (prerequisites first;
the luxury marker is the book's luxury pick, skipped once we have one); the first tree
stays eFirstPolicyBranch. City log: "STRIKE LIST - ...".

